1. DEFINITIONS

"Engine" means Reverie itself: its source code, object code, headers,
build scripts, build configuration, documentation, the command-line
tools shipped with it (reverie, revtool), and the engine assets it
ships (including the bundled example themes), in whole or in part, in
original or modified form.

"Wallpaper Content" means wallpaper material created by an author that
is displayed by the Engine. Wallpaper Content includes `.rev` scene
files, theme folders and `.revpack` theme packages, and the images,
videos, SVG artwork, and other assets those wallpapers embed or
reference. Wallpaper Content does NOT include the Engine itself, any
modified version of the Engine, or any part of the Engine.

"Engine Copy" means a binary form of the Engine that Wallpaper Content
needs to be present at run time in order to be displayed — for
example, the reverie and revtool executables installed on an end
user's system, or a package (.deb, .rpm, .pkg.tar.zst, .apk, .xbps)
containing them. An Engine Copy is and remains part of the Engine, not
part of Wallpaper Content, wherever it is installed, however it is
obtained, and whoever installs it.

"Licensor" means FemBoyGamerTechGuy, the copyright holder of the
Engine, identified here by the established project handle under which
the Engine is authored and published.

"You" means any individual or entity that obtains access to the
Engine, in any form and through any channel.

"Written Authorization" means an express, written permission issued
by the Licensor for a specific act or set of acts. This license
itself is one such authorization, for the acts it expressly permits.

