repository. All rights not expressly granted in Section 4 are
reserved by the Licensor.

This license grants no rights in the Licensor's names, marks, logos,
or branding, including "Reverie", "Reverie Engine", and "Faded
Dream".

3. SCOPE — WHAT THIS LICENSE GOVERNS

This license governs the Engine and the materials expressly covered
by it. It does NOT automatically govern Wallpaper Content. A `.rev`
wallpaper, theme package, or media wallpaper you create with the
Engine is YOUR work: it does not carry this license, and the Engine's
restrictions never attach to it, as further described in Section 5.

4. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to the terms of this license, the Licensor grants You a
limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

a. Download, install, and use the Engine, and to make the copies of
it (including backup copies) that are reasonably necessary to do so,
for the purpose of creating, testing, displaying, and enjoying
wallpapers on Your own systems;

b. Create Wallpaper Content with the Engine — scenes, themes, and
media wallpapers — including for distribution and sale, subject to
Section 5;

c. Distribute and commercially sell or otherwise exploit Your
Wallpaper Content, subject to Section 5; and

d. Rely on a separately installed Engine. Wallpaper Content You
distribute must consist of Your own scenes, assets, and media. You
may NOT bundle, embed, or otherwise include the Engine — or any
Engine Copy of it — in or with anything You distribute: not in or
with the wallpaper itself, its installer, a container or sandbox
image, an archive, or any other distribution artifact, unless the
Licensor first grants that permission in a further, specific Written
Authorization. End users obtain and install the Engine themselves —
from the Licensor or from a channel the Licensor authorizes (the
published release packages, or a build from this repository). Stating
that Your wallpaper requires the Reverie Engine, or directing users
to an authorized channel for it, is permitted and does not constitute
distributing the Engine.

5. WALLPAPER CONTENT AND AUTHOR RIGHTS

a. Wallpaper Content is an independent work. To the maximum extent
permitted by applicable law, this license claims no rights over
Wallpaper Content, and the Licensor neither owns nor co-owns a
wallpaper by virtue of its author having used the Engine to create
or display it.

b. Creating a `.rev` wallpaper, theme, or media wallpaper with the
Engine does NOT carry this license to the wallpaper. You retain all
rights in and to Your Wallpaper Content — the scene files, the theme
packages, the images, videos, and SVG artwork — and You may
distribute, license, sell, or otherwise exploit them under terms You
choose, subject to applicable law, to any separate agreements that
bind You, and to the licenses of any third-party components You
include in them. The ownership runs one way: Your wallpapers are
Yours; the Engine is not.

c. Wallpaper Content does not become the property of the Licensor or
of the Faded Dream Project merely because it targets the Engine. The
restrictions of Section 6 attach to the Engine, never to Your
wallpaper files or their assets.

d. Nothing in this license limits Your right to state factually that
Your wallpaper is made with, or runs on, Reverie. However, You may
not name, brand, or market Your wallpaper in a way that states or
implies that it IS the Engine, that it is part of the Faded Dream
Project, or that the Licensor endorses it, without prior Written
Authorization.

e. The boundary: if You extract, adapt, or republish Engine code,
Engine components, or the Engine's shipped assets (including its
bundled example themes) outside of Wallpaper Content — for example,
as another engine, framework, library, template, or standalone asset
collection — that act is governed by Section 6, not by this Section.

f. The separate-Engine rule in Section 4(d) is a limit on what You
may distribute of the Engine, never on Your Wallpaper Content. A
theme that requires a separately installed Reverie Engine is none
the less complete, independent, and fully distributable under this
Section, and nothing in that rule restricts Your wallpaper's own
packaging, installer, pricing, distribution channels, or terms — so
long as the artifact You distribute does not itself contain or
accompany the Engine or an Engine Copy.

